From: =?UTF-8?q?Andr=C3=A9=20Braga?= <code@andrebraga.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ROCKNIX: drm/msm/a8xx: also accept the 44050000 id for Adreno 830

The upstream A830 entry matches the DT compatible "qcom,adreno-44050001".
Mesa before 26.3 ("freedreno: Add chip-id support for A830v1") only
knows the msm id as 0xffff44050000, so x86 userspace under FEX, whose
Mesa comes from a distro rootfs we don't ship, falls back to llvmpipe
on the upstream id. The Odin 3 DT selects 44050000 instead; it is the
same GPU, and the GMU gets its id from .gmu_chipid either way.

chip_ids[0] stays 0x44050001, so the adreno_is_*() checks are unchanged.
Drop this, and the &gpu override in cq8725s-ayn-odin3.dts, once the x86
rootfs Mesa on installed devices is 26.3 or later.
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/adreno/a6xx_catalog.c
@@ -2687,7 +2687,7 @@
 
 static const struct adreno_info a8xx_gpus[] = {
 	{
-		.chip_ids = ADRENO_CHIP_IDS(0x44050001),
+		.chip_ids = ADRENO_CHIP_IDS(0x44050001, 0x44050000),
 		.family = ADRENO_8XX_GEN1,
 		.fw = {
 			[ADRENO_FW_SQE] = "gen80000_sqe.fw",
